homr-web is a port to TypeScript of homr, "Homer's Optical Music Recognition",
by Christian Liebhardt, https://github.com/liebharc/homr, licensed under the
GNU Affero General Public License version 3. This port reproduces homr
release 0.7.0 (commit 8b5dcf7d7bdd1a47911dc0c661c573b957271eab) and is
distributed under the same licence; see LICENSE.

The models the port runs are homr's own, downloaded unchanged from the homr
"onnx_checkpoints" release and identified by name and SHA-256 in
test/golden/*/meta.json. homr builds on:

- oemer, https://github.com/BreezeWhite/oemer, MIT licence: the
  segmentation models.
- Polyphonic-TrOMR, https://github.com/NetEase/Polyphonic-TrOMR, Apache
  licence 2.0: the transformer.

Their authors ask that research use cite them.

At run time the port loads, as ordinary npm dependencies under their own
licences: onnxruntime-web (MIT), @techstark/opencv-js, a build of OpenCV
(Apache licence 2.0), and delaunator (ISC) with robust-predicates (Unlicense).

The chord and title OCR ports parts of two more works:

- RapidOCR, https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR, Apache licence 2.0: the
  pipeline of release 3.9.2 (preprocessing, DBPostProcess, the classifier
  and recogniser batching, CTC decoding), itself derived from PaddleOCR,
  https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR, Apache licence 2.0. Its three
  models, PP-OCRv6 small detection and recognition and the v2.0 mobile
  direction classifier, are PaddleOCR's, Apache licence 2.0, served
  unchanged as rapidocr ships them.
- Clipper 6.4.2 by Angus Johnson, http://www.angusj.com/delphi/clipper.php,
  Boost Software Licence 1.0: the polygon offset with round joins
  (src/ocr/clipper-offset.ts).
